# Python sources are LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the
# index. Without this, git's core.autocrlf=true checks them out as CRLF on
# Windows, and any tool that later writes LF into one leaves the file with
# mixed endings - which `ruff format --check .` reports as needing reformatting
# even though the committed content is fine and CI (which checks out LF) is
# green. Found 2026-08-27 in llm_client.py and test_llm_client.py.
#
# Deliberately scoped to *.py: nothing here forces an ending on files that may
# genuinely need CRLF.
*.py text eol=lf
